	(text "CONNECTORS (Node60 harness page; REQ-NET-001: exactly four node conductors: T1S pair, battery, ground)\nAll connector parts are PLACEHOLDERS (generic symbols) until the mating sets are selected and frozen together:\n  housings, terminals, seals, wire sizes and keys (harness page, connector freeze condition).\nJ901 battery input: Metri-Pack 480/630 class, or a dual feed with each feed fused; prove the full 60 A path.\nJ902 power return: matched high-current return; no chassis-only return.\n  Fuse: primary fuse at the battery/source end (off-board); per-feed fuses if dual-fed.\nJ903 T1S: separate sealed two-way twisted pair. ESD (D501/D502) sits right behind this connector (DEC-012).\nJ904-J909 outputs: TE Deutsch DT13-2P right-angle headers, one per output (DEC-013 replaces the MX150 plan),\n  10 A per output, 14 AWG minimum; validate contact derating at +125 C. Mating plug DT06-2S.\nNo KL15, ignition or local wake input (DEC-007).\nUNVERIFIED (release-blocking): every connector mate, pinout and current rating.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "21d611b3-b87a-549e-9cd6-72260cdd441f")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
